@page "/lessons/names"
@attribute [RouteName("l2")]
@attribute [RouteTitle("Names instead of URLs")]

<LessonFrame Number="2">
    <Try>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li>Pick a route name in the <b>URL forge</b> and fill in its values. The URL is built from the name, never typed by hand.</li>
            <li>Type <code>abc</code> where an <code>int</code> is expected. The router refuses and says why, before anything navigates.</li>
            <li>Try <b>beacon</b>: its second value is optional, so the URL is shorter when you leave it empty.</li>
            <li>Use the two launch buttons. They reach the same page; one passes a name and values, the other calls a method the
                compiler checks.</li>
        </ol>
    </Try>
    <Stage>
        <div class="forge">
            <div class="forge-pick">
                <label for="forge-route">Route name</label>
                <select id="forge-route" value="@Selected" @onchange="OnPick">
                    @foreach (var name in Names)
                    {
                        <option value="@name">@name</option>
                    }
                </select>
                <span class="forge-template mono">@Template</span>
            </div>

            @if (Parameters.Count == 0)
            {
                <p class="dim">This route has no values to fill in.</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="forge-values">
                    @foreach (var parameter in Parameters)
                    {
                        <label class="forge-field">
                            <span>@parameter.Name <small>@parameter.Rule</small></span>
                            <input type="text" value="@Values.GetValueOrDefault(parameter.Name)"
                                   placeholder="@(parameter.Optional ? "optional" : "required")"
                                   @oninput="e => SetValue(parameter.Name, e.Value?.ToString())" />
                        </label>
                    }
                </div>
            }

            <div class="forge-out @(Error is null ? "ok" : "bad")" aria-live="polite">
                @if (Error is null)
                {
                    <span class="forge-label">Built URL</span>
                    <code class="forge-url">@Url</code>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="forge-label">Refused</span>
                    <span class="forge-error">@Error</span>
                }
            </div>

            <div class="forge-actions">
                <button class="btn" disabled="@(Error is not null)" @onclick="Launch">Launch with the name</button>
                <button class="btn btn-quiet" @onclick="LaunchTyped">Dock 4, the typed way</button>
            </div>
            <p class="dim forge-note">
                The typed way is <code>await Navigation.NavigateToDockAsync(4)</code>. It exists because the page <code>L2Dock</code> declares
                <code>[RouteName("dock")]</code>; a mistake in the name or the value type is a compile error.
            </p>
        </div>

        <XRay Name="Lesson2Page" Level="0">
            <ModRouterOutlet>
                <EmptyContent><p class="dim">Launch a route to see its page here.</p></EmptyContent>
            </ModRouterOutlet>
        </XRay>
    </Stage>
    <Code>
        <CodeRef File="Lessons/L2/Lesson2Page.razor">a page that declares its route with <code>@@page</code> and <code>[RouteName]</code></CodeRef>
        <CodeRef File="Lessons/L2/Lesson2Page.razor.cs"><code>TryGetRouteUrl</code>, <code>NavigateToRoute</code> and the generated typed helper</CodeRef>
        <CodeRef File="Lessons/L2/L2Dock.razor">a child page that nests under its parent with <code>[RouteParent]</code></CodeRef>
        <CodeRef File="LabRoutes.cs"><code>AddPages</code> finds the attribute pages next to the fluent routes</CodeRef>
    </Code>
</LessonFrame>
